# Intent: The control sheet at finger size (owner review 2026-11-18, the physical standard in docs/design/screen-style.md; batch UX13c, brief docs/plan/ux13c-control-sheet-brief.md). The sheet has a fixed height (208 px) and two pages. Page 1 is the status row (Wi-Fi bars, the time, the battery) and the two sliders as 304 by 56 px rows, 8 px apart: the name in the 20 px text over its value in 16 px at the left, the track at the right, the whole row the grab area. Page 2 is the tiles, two rows of three, each 96 by 56 px with 8 px gaps and margins, the icon above a 16 px word, with the one line of status text above them. A 48 px strip at the bottom holds the page dots and an 80 by 48 px Next / Back target. A fresh open starts on page 1. The older mpg_sheet_layout stays for the config tests; the drawing uses the new mpg_sheet2_layout. The swipe left and right between the sheet pages is not in this patch (a slider drag looks like a swipe; to settle on the unit). Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_pages.cc, maipai_pages_core.h (ours)
# Check after a flash: the sheet opens on the sliders and the status row; each slider moves from anywhere along its row; Next shows the six tiles, each easy to press, with a gap between them; Back returns; the dots show the page; Mute and Quiet still fill when on; Apps, Games, Lock and the gear work as before.
# Kconfig: none

